## SOA vs Microservices

| Aspect | SOA | Microservices |
|--------|-----|---------------|
| **Scope** | Enterprise-wide | Application-specific |
| **Granularity** | Larger services (business domains) | Fine-grained services |
| **Communication** | ESB-centric | Direct communication/APIs |
| **Data** | Shared databases | Independent databases |
| **Coupling** | Moderate | Loose |
| **Deployment** | Often monolithic deployment | Independent deployment |
| **Complexity** | Medium | High |
| **Organization** | Centralized | Team-based ownership |
| **Performance** | Can be slower (ESB overhead) | Optimized per service |
| **Maturity** | Established | Modern/Evolving |

### Migration Path
```
Monolithic Application
        ↓
Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA)
        ↓
Microservices Architecture
```

**SOA acts as a bridge** to modularization before full microservices adoption.

